<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.T2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Benchmark Results of Post-trained LLMs.<span id="S3.T2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> LLaDA only employs an SFT procedure, while other models have extra reinforcement learning (RL) alignment. <sup id="S3.T2.8.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S3.T2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup> indicates models are evaluated under the same protocol, detailed in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS6" title="B.6 Standard Benchmarks and Evaluation Details ‣ Appendix B Experiments ‣ Large Language Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>. Results indicated by <sup id="S3.T2.8.1.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S3.T2.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> and <sup id="S3.T2.8.1.3" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S3.T2.8.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">¶</span></sup> are sourced from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. [26]</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bi et al. [32]</a></cite> respectively. The numbers in parentheses represent the number of shots used for in-context learning. “-” indicates unknown data.</span></span></figcaption>
